<title>USA: TABLE-Carolina State Bank Q2 net shr flat.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Carolina State Bank Q2 net shr flat.</headline>
<dateline>SHELBY, N.C. 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 MONTHS</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr		  $0.23		    $0.23</p>
<p> Net		  $361		     $359</p>
<p> Avg shrs	   1,599,983		$1,598,733</p>
<p>		     6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		  $0.39		    $0.40</p>
<p> Net		  $624		     $635</p>
<p> Avg shrs	   1,599,983		$1,598,733</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Total assets for in Q2 1997 were $141,489,000 compared to $125,026,000 during the same period last year.</p>
<p>Total deposits in Q2 1997 were $120,647,000 compared to $105,813,000 during the same period last year.</p>
<p>As previously reported on June 30, 1997, Carolina State bank has signed a letter of intent to be acquired by First Charter Corp, headquartered in Concord, N.C. for $38.3 million or roughly $22.25 for each Carolina State Bank share.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the new bank would have assets of approximately $700 million.</p>
